  "real_world_anchor": {
    "primary": "Two ice skaters pushing apart on a rink. A light skater and a heavy skater press palms and push — one shove, and BOTH glide away at the same instant; the lighter one always leaves faster, yet neither pushed harder.",
    "secondary": "A swimmer's turn — pushing off the pool wall. You push the wall, the wall's equal push is what launches you; the wall never moves because its body is the Earth."
  },
